    "updated_at": "2016-12-08T22:21:57Z",
    "body": "Oops, thanks for correcting the test case.\r\n\r\n> Perform a security check on what?\r\n\r\nI don't know. I'm still trying to wrap my head around how these things work. Per your comment above and https://github.com/w3c/browser-payment-api/issues/361#issuecomment-265814366 I take it that the security check wouldn't make sense for constructors, but active document check makes sense. But not for all constructors. `Date` or `Image` are not problematic for example. OK. Let's close this and discuss `PaymentRequest` in the other issue.",
